  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Florida International University is a public research university situated in Miami, Florida. Established in 1965, it is one of the largest universities in Florida and offers over 190 degree programs in a vast range of fields.<br><br>More than 3500 international students from over 140 countries come together to study at Florida International University, with around 58,00 students enrolled altogether. The university is recognized for its research discoveries in environmental studies, STEM fields, and social sciences.</p><p>Various research centers and institutes can be found across the campus, too as the university is famed for its capacity to facilitate research in several areas. Notably, the Stocker AstroScience Center has a 24-inch telescope. Computing and technology resources are surplus, with online learning platforms and technical support services provided to empower students in their studies.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>Florida International University on-campus housing varies in cost according to the type of accommodation chosen. The dormitories are designed to provide students with a secure living space as each room is fully furnished with a desk, bed, dressing room tables etc. Residential facilities are separated into the MMC (Modesto A. Maidique Campus) and the BBC (Biscayne Bay Campus). The MMC houses seven residential halls, while the BBC has four residence halls.</p><p>On-campus apartments incorporate Parkview Hall and University Apartments and feature a kitchenette, living room and two or four private bedrooms. Suite-style apartments offer additional privacy if desired.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Library",
      "value": "<p>Florida International University contains multiple libraries, including the Hubert Library on the BBC campus and the Green Library on the MMC campus. Both libraries house a sizable collection of books and journals for students to peruse, in addition to computer labs, study areas and more.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student Life",
      "value": "<p>Student life is only complete when you get involved with the student union. The two student unions are named the Wolfe University Center on the BBC campus and The Graham Center on the MMC campus. Both offer a range of resources, including meeting rooms, dining options and event spaces.</p><p>Students can go green on a 3-mile running nature trail, relax in the butterfly gardens or have some fun competing in the Walk On Water race. These are just some examples of the events students can attend on campus, not to mention the 300+ organizations dotted around campus, from cultural clubs and honors societies and beyond.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
